TITLE:: RLMorphism
summary:: A map between two contexts that their transformations go through: temperaments, pushed and lifted walks
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLChordContext, Classes/RLWalk, Classes/RLJust, Classes/RLEDO, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A morphism sends each chord of a strong::source:: context to a chord of a strong::target:: context so that, for every name both contexts know, moving then mapping is mapping then moving: code::map(P(x)) == P(map(x))::. link::#-isValid:: checks it.

Such a map carries walks forward (link::#-push::) and, the other way, lifts them (link::#-lift::): a walk of the target and a chord above its start give the walk above it, by the same word.

A strong::temperament:: is the first example (link::#*temper::): the val of an equal division sends the just lattice's triads onto the division's. Every closed walk of the division lifts to a just walk that ends a comma away, a comma the division tempers out. What the walk hides in the division, the lift shows.

code::
~just = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLJust([3, 5])));
~edo = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12)));
~temper = RLMorphism.temper(~just, ~edo);
~temper.(~just.space.minor([-1, 1]));       // A minor
~temper.isValid;                             // true, on a patch of the lattice

~hexatonic = RLWalk.cycle(~edo, ~edo.space.major(0), [\P, \L]);
~above = ~temper.lift(~hexatonic);           // from 1/1 major
~above.drift;                                // [0, -3]
~just.system.commaName(~above.drift);        // diesis 128/125
~temper.push(~above) == ~hexatonic;          // true

// a map that is no morphism
RLMorphism(~edo, ~edo, { |chord| ~edo.space.chord(chord.root * 2, chord.type) }).isValid;   // false
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: source
argument:: target
Two contexts.
argument:: map
A Function, chord of the source -> chord of the target.
argument:: label

METHOD:: temper
The temperament from a just context to an equal division's: roots through the val, types kept. Any other pair of systems is an Error.
argument:: source
A context on an link::Classes/RLJust::.
argument:: target
A context on an link::Classes/RLEDO::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: source
METHOD:: target
METHOD:: map
METHOD:: label

METHOD:: value
The chord a chord goes to. code::morphism.(chord)::.

METHOD:: isValid
Whether the map commutes with every transformation the two contexts both name.
argument:: sample
The chords to check on: every chord of a finite source, a patch round the origin of a lattice (exponents -3 to 3), when nil.

METHOD:: push
A walk of the source, carried to the target.

METHOD:: lift
A walk of the target, lifted to the source.
argument:: walk
argument:: from
A chord above the walk's start (one the map sends to it; anything else is an Error); the source's base chord of the start's type when nil.
